# Crux — release signing credentials.
#
# 1. Copy this file to `android/key.properties` (that path is git-ignored).
# 2. Generate an upload keystore ONCE and never lose it — losing it means you
#    can no longer update the app under the same Play listing:
#
#      keytool -genkey -v -keystore %USERPROFILE%\crux-upload.jks \
#        -storetype JKS -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -validity 10000 \
#        -alias crux
#
#    (On macOS/Linux use ~/crux-upload.jks and a forward-slash path below.)
# 3. Back the .jks file up somewhere safe and private (password manager /
#    encrypted drive). It is NOT in this repo on purpose.
#
# Note: with Play App Signing (recommended, default for new apps) this key is
# your *upload* key. Google re-signs with the app signing key it holds, so a
# lost upload key can be reset via support — but keep it safe regardless.

storePassword=your-keystore-password
keyPassword=your-key-password
keyAlias=crux
# Absolute path, forward slashes on all platforms:
storeFile=C:/Users/you/crux-upload.jks
